learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T12:41:50.313Z","harness:claude-code","Treating an observation as a fallback is a design error that keeps recurring in identity code. resolveAuthorIdentity returns early as soon as a higher-precedence branch supplies an author, so detected harness — and soon the detected model — is computed only when nothing else answered. Precedence over WHICH value is authoritative is a separate question from whether an observation is worth recording: the assertion decides the author, the observation decides the provenance, and both belong in the entry. The general rule for any future precedence chain in this codebase: resolve the authoritative value by precedence, but record every cheap observation unconditionally, and keep a discriminator saying which is which."
body: ""
